    "precedent": "New York institutions already fund employee transportation at scale — intercampus shuttles, guaranteed-ride programs, tenant buses. One of the city's largest hospital systems already runs an employee water shuttle. The behavior is proven. What's been missing is a vessel built for it.",
    "stripe_lesson": "We ran the first employer water commute on San Francisco Bay. The ride worked; the vessel was the lesson — an 8-seat executive boat is not a commuter line. The 20-seat N45 is built for exactly this: a scheduled line your team can set a watch by, with a seat that works like a desk.",
    "product_n30": "N30 Executive Shuttle — 8 seats, on-demand, available now. For leadership teams, airport runs, and client moves.",
    "product_n45": "N45 Commuter Line — 20 seats, scheduled service on a fixed line. Launches when a line reaches roughly 60–72 committed seats.",
    "loi_cta": "Two ways to bring a line to your people. Option A — sponsor a line: your institution underwrites a scheduled service, your name on the hull optional (indicative from ~$125K per month). Option B — commit seats: reserve seats at $750–900 per seat-month and we aggregate your line's launch. Both start with a non-binding letter of intent: it costs nothing, commits nothing, and tells us which line to build first.",
    "footer_note": "Letters of intent are non-binding."
